"""Pure-Python font width metrics for summary layout estimation.

Replaces the former ReportLab ``stringWidth`` dependency. The per-character
advance-width tables below were extracted once from the Adobe standard-14
AFM metrics (via ReportLab's ``getFont(name).widths`` data) for Helvetica,
Helvetica-Bold, and Times-Roman, expressed in 1/1000ths of an em.

The summary pages are rendered by headless Chromium with the vendored
delivery fonts (Public Sans / Fraunces / IBM Plex Mono), whose advance
widths were extracted from the font files themselves and appear in the
measured tables below. Callers that use these estimates to budget page
heights should still inflate the result with a safety factor (see
``SAFETY_FACTOR``) — Chromium applies kerning and shaping that the
per-glyph sums don't model — so estimates over-predict and rendered
pages never overflow.
"""

from typing import Dict, Mapping

#: Conservative multiplier applied by layout estimators on top of the raw
#: per-glyph width sums, covering kerning/shaping differences in Chromium's
#: actual text layout. Tuned against side-by-side Chromium renders.
SAFETY_FACTOR = 1.06

